the Queen's coffin will leave in  procession followed by members of the  royal family led by the Queen's four  children including the king  to the sound of minute guns the  procession will carry the queen along  the mall for the last time  before turning right into horse guards  parade  with Big Ben tolling every minute the  procession will cross the great  ceremonial parade ground sight of  trooping the color on the Queen's  official birthday each year  then turning onto Whitehall it will  travel past some of the great offices of  government Downing Street and the  cenotaph which commemorates the nation's  War dead  entering Parliament Square the  procession will turn into New Palace  yard in front of the houses of  Parliament  and then into Westminster Hall where the  Queen's coffin will be taken to Lion  State for the days before her funeral  the procession will make its way into  the oldest part of the Palace of  Westminster led by Heralds and then the  most senior figures in Parliament the  palace and the church of England  the coffin draped with the Royal  Standard will be placed on a raised  platform the catafalk in the middle of  Westminster Hall the king queen consort  and other members of the Royal Family  behind  after a short service led by the  Archbishop of Canterbury the procession  party will leave and members of the  Yeoman of the guard and the household  division will take up positions around  the coffin forming a vigil that will  guard the queen as she lies in state  until her funeral
 

